Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summary for boundary and initial conditions", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"16690147-38a6-487c-8261-54b59f072972"],

Cell["\<\
When setting up partial differential equations, it is important to be able to \
determine at exactly what locations initial and boundary conditions are \
required.  The location of these conditions is determined by the nature of \
the PDE.  Usually, if the physical problem and the corresponding PDE are in \
agreement, then the initial and boundary conditions required to give meaning \
to the physical problem will be identical to those required to give meaning \
to the mathematical problem.  Therefore a better understanding of the \
mathematical representation goes hand in hand with the better understanding \
of the physical problem.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2c8b5de1-119a-49b9-81b7-4e548c56929a"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Example: pollution and oxygen concentrations:", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7b397aac-a377-46da-bb0e-5d5e40097e66"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Remove", "[", "\"\<Global`*\>\"", " ", "]"}], " "}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1709]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f205da0a-faf0-4d1b-951b-d2e6af72bdcf"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Construction of the PDE model:", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"b0b7adfe-6072-4c62-83a8-cbce6c472996"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bacterial decomposition of the pollutant requires an uptake of \
dissolved oxygen in the water.  As the pollutant is degraded, oxygen is used \
up.  Let:\n\n\t\[Delta][x,t]  =  Density of dissolved oxygen in the river\n\n\
\t\[Delta]m  =  Its maximum value, which depends on temperature\n\nAssume \
that the rate \[Mu] at which the oxygen is consumed is the same as that of \
pollutant decay (also \[Mu]) and is proportional to the pollutant \
concentration.  This represents a sink term and is given as:\n\n\tk1[x,t]  =  \
- \[Mu] \[Rho][x,t]\n\nThere is also a source term for the oxygen \
concentration due to the fact that the river surface, in contact with the air \
above, draws oxygen in from the atmosphere by a process known as \
re-oxygenation.  Assume that this happens at a rate proportional to the \
difference between the saturation level  \[Delta]m  and the actual oxygen \
concentration \[Delta].  Thus:\n\n\tk2[x,t]  =   \[Mu]1 ( \[Delta]m  -  \
\[Delta][x,t] )\n\t\nFinally, assume that the oxygen concentration obeys the \
basic conservation PDE equation.  Specifically, the internal flux (left and \
right) occurs by advection with the river velocity c.  Thus:\n\n \t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", "\[Delta]", " ", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"6bbf9333-6b18-4e46-9c31-15de63eaa5b9"],
 "  =  -",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", "q", "  ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"bcdc5634-fbfd-4e88-9156-a99339a0867e"],
 "  +  k\n \t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", "\[Delta]", " ", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"d83677d0-e35c-499e-b9cf-0721548f9a9c"],
 "  =  -",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", 
      RowBox[{"c", "  ", "\[Delta]"}], "  ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"ce426a93-e040-4969-8cca-ecf0ed01bad9"],
 "  +  k1 + k2\n \t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", "\[Delta]", " ", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"331e369b-9a83-41dc-9c0c-708f97844501"],
 "  =  - c ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", "\[Delta]", " ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"63355805-1d67-4010-a558-7c640c9651a4"],
 "   - \[Mu] \[Rho]   +   \[Mu]1 ( \[Delta]m  -  \[Delta] )\n \t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Delta]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], " ", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"e285ca1b-f511-4249-951c-cbec178247e1"],
 "  =  - c ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Delta]", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], " ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"3771ce9d-c390-44ed-abbd-272be5b1e627"],
 "   - \[Mu] \[Rho][x,t]   +   \[Mu]1 ( \[Delta]m  -  \[Delta][x,t] )\n \t \n\
Also, recall that the PDE for the pollutant density is:\n\n \t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"2447d6f0-1105-4f5f-af97-7b2bef673e0c"],
 "  =  -",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"c", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
      RowBox[{"(", "  ", "\[Rho]", "  ", ")"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"729c35a3-d877-49af-9083-ff259bbd85df"],
 "  -  \[Mu] \[Rho]\n\t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], " ", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"1f17937f-fe6f-4623-ab38-68ea37e91ad1"],
 "  =  - c ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
     RowBox[{"(", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], "  ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"dc0e95b0-82a1-4876-b693-cf51e08fc252"],
 "  -  \[Mu] \[Rho][x,t]  \n\nTherefore, the resulting PDE system (pollution \
density and oxygen concentration) satisfy the two conservation PDEs:\n\n\t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], " ", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"c85596ac-b125-4f57-b7a9-b689ec3245c9"],
 "  =  - c ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
     RowBox[{"(", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], "  ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"247035fe-43db-4490-8b51-ce30f214eb85"],
 "  -  \[Mu] \[Rho][x,t]  \n \t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Delta]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], " ", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"eba9dc2e-0a6c-4e37-8c1c-caf496cebc5e"],
 "  =  - c ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
     RowBox[{"(", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Delta]", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], "  ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"30256b7e-564a-451f-95fb-cf1aef179be0"],
 "   -  \[Mu] \[Rho][x,t]   +   \[Mu]1 ( \[Delta]m  -  \[Delta][x,t] )"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e64e5dfc-5de2-44d9-ab3f-0ca3dd5ffa0c"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Initial and boundary conditions:", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"9fcda757-b23e-481f-9409-70f1dec7fdd5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The initial and boundary conditions required by each of our PDEs will be \
the same because both PDEs have the same form, and therefore the same \
characteristic curves.  Because our velocity is positive from left to right, \
then the characteristic curves in the space-time domain slope to the right.  \
Therefore, both PDEs require initial and left (i.e. entrance) boundary \
conditions.\n\nAlthough more complicated boundary and initial conditions can \
be specified, only the following simple case will be illustrated here.\n\n\
Assume that a pollutant is being dumped into the river at location ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ecc639d7-47c4-495f-b7ad-3a44f0affbaa"],
 " starting at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"t", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "61b06cb5-fb85-49d1-a1b9-141de6fd85d7"],
 " in such a manner that the density goes from 0 to 1 in a short interval of \
time, and then becomes almost constant.  Specifically, the left (i.e. \
entrance) boundary condition is:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", "t"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", ".5"}], "t"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "243fe599-1ef6-4dc0-aafa-bdb0b2606312"],
 "\n\nNext, assume that the the river is clean downstream at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"t", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c429f89b-6b1c-4d1c-8d54-ec650cfe4db6"],
 " (i.e. the downstream density is zero at the beginning time). \n\n\t\
\[Rho][x,0] = 0\n\nLikewise, assume that both the initial oxygen \
concentration and the inlet boundary oxygen concentration are both equal to \
2.0.  This case corresponds to a clean oxygenated river upstream of the \
pollution at all times:\n\n\t\[Delta][0,t] = 2\n\nas well as a clean \
oxygenated river downstream of the pollution point before the pollution is \
dumped into the river:\n\n\t\[Delta][x,0] = 2\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.466269905594281*^9, 
  3.466269925563031*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"093b59ea-c0bd-4375-a975-\
b1ae5d71b911"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Numerical solution:", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"7620e7aa-5c82-4225-b69f-0ae3e4e1abcc"],

Cell["\<\
The remaining parameters required by the model include the pollutant decay \
rate and the re-oxygenation rate.  For our first example set the \
re-oxygenation rate 50 percent higher than the pollutant decay rate.  Also, \
set the maximum oxygen concentration to be the same as the initial oxygen \
concentration in the river.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2a796acf-99ed-43a5-99e4-554050e725cb"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", ".20"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Mu]", " ", "=", " ", ".1"}], ";"}], "        ", 
  RowBox[{"(*", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"i", ".", "e", ".", " ", "with"}], " ", "decay"}], "  ", 
   "*)"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Mu]1", " ", "=", " ", ".15"}], ";"}], "   ", 
  RowBox[{"(*", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"i", ".", "e", ".", " ", "with"}], " ", "re"}], "-", 
    "oxygenation"}], "  ", "*)"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Delta]m", " ", "=", " ", "2"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"L", " ", "=", " ", "10"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tStop", " ", "=", " ", "50"}], ";"}]}], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1710]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2be85385-92f2-4670-a0b2-5971ec0b0aad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Examine the space dependent (i.e. initial) boundary condition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "0"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2d733343-408f-4644-a349-4e6efeb877bf"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3985121323123055`*^9, 3.3985121561560555`*^9}, {
  3.3985124343435555`*^9, 
  3.3985124386248055`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e032ff4b-5408-4344-84d2-\
02e6f768547c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"0", ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", "L"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".015", "]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
